OL,3,GNEWSAInvasive demon shrimp discovered
OL,4,Ain waterway
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn invasive species of shrimp has been
OL,7,Fdiscovered in a protected waterway,
OL,8,Fraising concerns for native species and
OL,9,Fthe wider ecosystem.
OL,11,FThe demon shrimp, larger than the
OL,12,Fnative equivalent and with a
OL,13,Fdistinctive stripy back, has been
OL,14,Fdiscovered in the Holy Brook, a
OL,15,Ftributary of the River Kennet which
OL,16,Fruns through Wiltshire and Berkshire.
OL,18,FThe charity Action for the River Kennet
OL,19,F(ARK) is urging those who encounter the
OL,20,Fspecies, which can outcompete native
OL,21,Fspecies, to report it to them.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,350,340,200,160,0,100
